A direct answer to the core question.

"Should I buy more?" — Not now.

The reason is simple. The 2026-05-28 report recommended selling **shs
immediately after the stop-loss (48,000KRW) was breached. That recommendation
has not been executed. Buying more into a position whose stop-loss has been
breached renders the stop-loss rule meaningless.

"It's fallen a lot = buying opportunity" only holds when the structural thesis
is intact. The structural demand for the AI power theme (US power grid, data
centers) has not been impaired. However, the problem is that there is no
immediate catalyst for a rebound right now. Rate direction is still uncertain,
and the LS ELECTRIC supply/demand shock is still in progress.

What should be done now:
Before reviewing additional purchases, the sequence is to first decide whether
to execute the prior recommendation (**shs sell). The choice is: honor the
stop-loss, or hold because you believe in the structural thesis — one of these
must be decided first. Both are rational choices, but buying more without
deciding either one violates risk management principles.
